      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": 8,
        "title": "We use comparisons when we want to state similarities or differences about people / places / objects / matters etc. Adjectives are used in this topic but they take a new form. Check the following examples.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "We use comparisons when we want to state similarities or differences about people / places / objects / matters etc. Adjectives are used in this topic but they take a new form. Check the following examples.",
          "Statements Questions Negative statements 1. Joe is more attractive than Kalvin Is Joe more attractive than Kalvin? Joe is not more attractive than Kalvin. 2. China is bigger than Japan. Is China bigger than Japan? China is not bigger than Japan. 3. Computers are more useful than TVs. Are computers more useful than TVs? Computers are not more useful than TVs."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
          {
            "url": "https://docs.google.com/slides-images-rt/AE1YXSbAo1AJLIIqPucExcXCbIXoBKbiMXI72ibj70esAlNgZmSwIutvD2WBjs-Y1lsoq_ZgvEG530rY_On4xVwTFH4paaF9i_O0bzDe9n_ZneGvsFPt9tAOOxTG6FnspvrHNLJwvGI8j_at1blqRLrJkKGKCYZjteFs45Xo7RaGS0kVI87MlTsSgIYO5kjXv4M=nw",
