      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "TO CONSIDER 1. Adjectives can be divided into two groups: / Short (1 or 2 syllables) / Long (2 or more syllables). 2. Short adjectives take the –er + than particles: Joe is taller than Jim. 3.Long adjectives take the more + than particles: It is more expensive here than there. 4.Short adjectives that finish in –y change to I + er: She is prettier than you. 5. There are irregular adjectives: Good – Better than / Bad – Worse than. 6. We use the particles ‘as / as’ to state similarities: Joe is as tall as Jake. 7. There are adjectives who do not receive comparison degrees; those adjective have absolute meaning: This is the final test / Those people are dead. 8. Less + Adjective + than is used to state inferiority between two nouns. E.G. Alex is less determined than his brother. 9. There are three levels of comparison: Superiority , Equality and Inferiority",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "TO CONSIDER 1. Adjectives can be divided into two groups: / Short (1 or 2 syllables) / Long (2 or more syllables). 2. Short adjectives take the –er + than particles: Joe is taller than Jim. 3.Long adjectives take the more + than particles: It is more expensive here than there. 4.Short adjectives that finish in –y change to I + er: She is prettier than you. 5. There are irregular adjectives: Good – Better than / Bad – Worse than. 6. We use the particles ‘as / as’ to state similarities: Joe is as tall as Jake. 7. There are adjectives who do not receive comparison degrees; those adjective have absolute meaning: This is the final test / Those people are dead. 8. Less + Adjective + than is used to state inferiority between two nouns. E.G. Alex is less determined than his brother. 9. There are three levels of comparison: Superiority , Equality and Inferiority"
        ],
