        "number": 11,
        "internalPageId": 10,
        "title": "Language Targets",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Language Targets",
          "Aspects Examples 1 State superiority He seems to be more interesting than his brother. 2 Express Equality These cars are as expensive as that truck. 3 Establish inferiority Your bag is less classy than mine. 4 Make general comparisons Both brothers are very alike. They don’t look the same to me.",
          "Comparisons can deal with different aspects. they can also be used at any tense.",
          "TO CONSIDER *This is a bigger city. *If you know the context, the comparison can be used without mentioning the other person /object / place / matter etc."
        ],
